\section{What Is Not Claimed}\label{sec:limits}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Consistent lies are invisible} (Theorem~\ref{thm:consistent-invisible}). Detecting an agent that is wrong but says so uniformly requires an independent source of truth (re-running the test, re-hashing the tree), not topology.
\item \textbf{Honest partitions are invisible} (Theorem~\ref{thm:partition-gauge}). Drift between internally consistent teams is a gauge shift. Detecting it requires a designated ground-truth agent or a fact whose value is pinned by a cryptographic anchor.
\item \textbf{Localisation is to cycles, not to agents.} $\rho$ is supported on cycles through the split-viewer; attribution within a cycle needs signed messages, at which point comparing an agent's outgoing messages directly is simpler than any projection. The value of the residual is that it works when the observer sees channel disagreements but not signed per-sender claims, and that it composes across channels the observer never inspected.
\item \textbf{Colluding agents on a common cycle can cancel} \cite{owens7}. The clique complex tightens this: if $H^1=0$ and the coalition preserves all triangle curls, its perturbation is gauge. That is a statement about chordal swarms, not about swarms in general.
\item \textbf{The greedy controller is not cost-optimal} and restores consistency by removing detection capacity.
\item \textbf{No live-LLM results are reported.} The previous draft's three seeds measured hash-folding artifacts. Re-running them under the fact registry is the first item of future work and will produce residuals in units of $\sqrt2$.
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}

Restricting the stalk to one-hot claims about registered facts, building the cochain from messages rather than states, and replacing declared 2-cells with the clique complex turns the previous draft's interpretive claims into three theorems with stated hypotheses: chordal swarms have no harmonic part, harmonic circulation in team-chordal swarms crosses team boundaries, and a split-view is triangle-witnessed exactly when the contradicted neighbour shares a further neighbour with the liar. The scalar $L$ survives as a per-edge topological constant that the operator can read off before any fault occurs. The price is honesty about scope: the detector certifies split-view lies and nothing else. Within that scope its guarantees are exact, it needs no noise model, and it costs one sparse solve.

